# Cloudflare Pages redirects (Netlify-compatible syntax).
# Cloudflare reads this file to configure redirects at the edge.
#
# The promoted build is index.html, which every static host serves at "/"
# automatically — so NO root rewrite is needed (and a root rewrite fought
# Cloudflare's automatic .html clean-URL handling, causing a 308 loop / 522).

# Versioned builds are no longer published at all — they live outside public/, which is the build
# output directory. This rule stays for links people may already have saved: an old
# /mi-dia-vNN.html now lands on the homepage instead of a 404. The hyphen means it does NOT match
# index.html. Best-effort on Cloudflare (a splat is a "dynamic" redirect).
/mi-dia-*      /              301
